        'ulip.rec.likely_surrender': '⚠️ <strong>LIKELY WORTH SURRENDERING.</strong> Policy IRR %1 is at or below FD rate. BTID projects <strong>%2</strong> vs <strong>%3</strong> — a surplus of <strong>%4</strong>. Note: continuing gives 80C tax benefit of ~%5 total — factor this in. <em>Buy term insurance first before surrendering.</em>',
        'ulip.rec.consider_surrender': '💡 <strong>CONSIDER SURRENDERING.</strong> BTID projects more wealth. However, policy IRR of %1 is above FD rate. Key question: is this cover (%2) your <em>only</em> life insurance? If yes, buy a term plan first. Also consider: 80C benefit of ~%3 reduces your effective cost if you stay.',
        'ulip.rec.continue': '✅ <strong>CONTINUE THE POLICY</strong> in this scenario. The policy maturity (%1) exceeds the BTID projection. However: <strong>never rely on an endowment policy as your primary life cover</strong> — buy a separate term plan. Also verify the maturity projection in your policy bond is realistic.',
        'ulip.rec.marginal': '💡 <strong>MARGINAL CASE.</strong> IRR of %1 and BTID advantage of %2. Decision depends on your other 80C investments, risk appetite, and whether this is your only life cover. Consult a SEBI-registered fee-only advisor before deciding.',
        'coffeecan.title':                         '☕ The Coffee Can',
        'coffeecan.what':                          '📖 What is Coffee Can Investing?',
        'coffeecan.disclaimer':                    '⚠ Disclaimer',
        'coffeecan.header.sub':              'Quality compounders · Buy &amp; hold 10+ years · Based on Saurabh Mukherjea / Marcellus framework',
        'coffeecan.what.desc':               'Coined by Robert Kirby (1984) and popularised in India by <strong>Saurabh Mukherjea (Marcellus Investment Managers)</strong> in <em>Coffee Can Investing: The Low Risk Road to Stupendous Wealth</em> (2018): lock high-quality businesses in a "coffee can" and forget them for 10 years. The philosophy demands companies with <strong>≥10% revenue CAGR</strong>, <strong>≥15% ROCE</strong> consistently over a decade, negligible debt, positive free cash flow every year, and stable promoter holdings — moat businesses that compound wealth without active management.',
        'coffeecan.metric.revcagr.sub':      '≥ 10% / 10 yr',
        'coffeecan.metric.roce.sub':         '≥ 15% avg',
        'coffeecan.metric.de.sub':           '≤ 1× preferred',
        'coffeecan.baserate.title':          'The Failure Rate — Read Before Investing',
        'coffeecan.baserate.sub':            'Passing a quality screen today does <strong>not</strong> guarantee outperformance. Here is what the data actually shows.',
